{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0037","billNumberShort":"H.B. 37","billNumberLong":"HB0037S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0821","shortTitle":"Used Oil Management Act Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"6","primeSponsor":"CHEWSH","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Chew, Scott H.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill makes changes to the Used Oil Management Act.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>increases the recycling fee on the sale of lubricating oil beginning on July 1, 2026;<hr><ltbullet>grants rulemaking authority to the Division of Waste Management and Radiation Control (division) to set the recycling fee on the sale of lubricating oil beginning on July 1, 2027;<hr><ltbullet>requires the division to notify the State Tax Commission of a fee change 90 days before the fee change goes into effect;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies that the division may use grant funding to hire permitted transporters as part of a curbside used oil collection program; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Ryan C. Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"TQOCSCQXXR","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-16 16:16:54.440","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-16 16:16:54.440","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assign